<title>CANADA: Canada March natural gas production falls 0.1 pct.</title>
<headline>Canada March natural gas production falls 0.1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Statistics Canada on Wednesday issued the following data for crude oil and natural gas production and exports:</p>
<p>CRUDE OIL AND EQUIVALENT HYDROCARBONS (thousand cubic meters)</p>
<p>		    Mar 1997     Mar 1996	 pct</p>
<p>   Production   9,884.4     10,060.3	 -1.7</p>
<p>   Exports	5,492.7	5,251.6	 +4.6</p>
<p>   Imports	3,869.2	3,863.0	 +0.2</p>
<p>   Ref receipts 8,276.8	8,478.3	 -2.4</p>
<p>NATURAL GAS (millions of cubic meters)</p>
<p>		   Mar 1997     Mar 1996	  pct</p>
<p>   Production  12,997.9     13,006.6	 -0.1</p>
<p>   Exports	7,480.0	6,704.5	+11.6</p>
<p>   Canada sales 7,326.9	7,219.8	 +1.5</p>
<p>CRUDE OIL (thousands of cubic meters)</p>
<p>		   Jan-Mar 1997  Jan-Mar 1996   pct</p>
<p>   Production     29,288.0   28,921.2	 1.3</p>
<p>   Exports	  16,477.2   15,731.3	 4.7</p>
<p>   Imports	  10,922.7   10,487.8	 4.1</p>
<p>   Ref receipts   24,047.3   23,854.4	 0.8</p>
<p>NATURAL GAS (milions of Cubic meters)</p>
<p>   Production     39,748.7   39,226.8	 1.3</p>
<p>   Exports	  21,490.9   20,320.6	 5.8</p>
<p>   Canada sales   23,197.6   23,287.1	-0.4</p>
<p>NOTE - Canada sales include direct sales.</p>
<p>(For more information from Statistics Canada, contact Gerard O'Connor, Energy Section, (613) 951-3562.)</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau (613) 235-6745))</p>
</text>
